\section{Branches}{

\itemize{
\item An \code{if} has two branches, \code{"TRUE"} and \code{"FALSE"}. The \code{"FALSE"} branch
of an \code{if} without an \verb{else} is taken when the condition is \code{FALSE}.
Nothing is recorded if the condition is \code{NA} or otherwise signals an
error.
\item A \code{switch()} has a branch for each of its arms, labelled with the name of
the arm. Arms that fall through to the next arm (\code{switch(x, a = , b = 1)})
share its branch, labelled \code{"a, b"}. An unnamed arm is labelled
\code{"<default>"}, or with its position if all arms are unnamed. A \code{switch()}
without a default arm has another branch, \code{"<no match>"}, taken when no
arm matches, including a number that selects no arm. A \code{switch()} with
arms in \code{...} has no branches.
}

\code{&&}, \code{||} and loops have no branches, nor does compiled code.

If the line where an \code{if} or \code{switch()} starts is excluded, e.g. with
\verb{# nocov} (see \link{exclusions}), all its branches are excluded too.
}

\section{Results}{


The branches are in the \code{branches} attribute of the coverage object, a list
with an element for each \code{if} and \code{switch()}, named like the elements of
the coverage object (see \link{coverage}). Each is a list with the \code{srcref} of
the \code{if} or \code{switch()}, its \code{functions}, the \code{labels} of its branches, and
\code{value}, the number of times each branch was taken. Use
\code{tally_coverage(by = "branch")} for a data frame with one row for each
branch, and \code{percent_coverage(by = "branch")} for the percentage of
branches taken.

\code{\link[=to_lcov]{to_lcov()}}, \code{\link[=to_cobertura]{to_cobertura()}}, \code{\link[=codecov]{codecov()}} and \code{\link[=coveralls]{coveralls()}} include the
branches. Codecov shows a line with branches that weren't all taken as
partly covered, and counts it as not covered in the coverage percentage, so
the percentage on Codecov is lower with branch coverage. \code{\link[=report]{report()}},
\code{\link[=file_report]{file_report()}} and \code{\link[=to_sonarqube]{to_sonarqube()}} don't include the branches yet.
}

